%N A402355 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n unlabeled nodes that are reducible as a flow graph rooted at every node.
%C A402355 The unlabeled counterpart of A400123. All digraphs have no self-loops; no root is distinguished in the isomorphism classes.
%C A402355 Equivalently, after deleting any node x, each remaining strongly connected component has at most one node receiving edges from outside that component in the original digraph. Such digraphs on n>=1 nodes have at most 2*(n-1) edges and are closed under simultaneous reversal of all edges.
%C A402355 For 1 <= n <= 5, a(n) = A109283(n-1), giving the common prefix 1, 1, 3, 15, 96. However, a(6) = 812 while A109283(5) = 735; no identity with that sequence is asserted.
%D A402355 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A402355 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A402355 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A402355 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A402355 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A402355 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A402355/b402355.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..29</a>
%H A402355 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A397968/a397968.py.txt">Required Python module (unlabeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Aug 2026.
%H A402355 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A402355 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A402355 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Required Python module (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%H A402355 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A399885/a399885.py.txt">Python program (unlabeled_reducible_elections.py)</a>, Nov 2026.
%F A402355 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{sigma in S_n} F(sigma), where S_n is the group of permutations of the n nodes and F(sigma) counts strongly connected loopless labeled digraphs fixed by sigma that satisfy the single-deletion condition in the comments.
